
KNOMI reference tests

Run the current Python model regressions from the repository root:

	python -m unittest discover -s test -p test_derive_prototype.py -v

Sixteen tests cover heater first-reach/priority/rearm, readiness, calibration/result
precedence and error visibility. Fourteen printer JSONL captures have reviewed
same-stem expected.txt files. Replay with:

	python -c "import glob; from tools.derive_prototype import main; main(sorted(glob.glob('test/fixtures/*.jsonl')))"

Expected files describe pre-debounce logical states, not physical screen timing.
Do not regenerate accepted baselines merely to hide a failure; review the trace.

Asset checks: python tools/check_assets.py --compile
Original UI rendering: tools/screen_reference/README.md
Firmware build: README.md (ESP-IDF 5.5.5, not PlatformIO).

Native C++ tests now include the Phase 2 hardware-rotation register mapping.
With CMake/Ninja and the existing portable Zig host compiler available:

	cmake -S test -B build/native -G Ninja -DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=<zig.exe> -DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER_ARG1=c++
	cmake --build build/native
	ctest --test-dir build/native --output-on-failure

For another native C++ compiler, use a separate build directory and omit the
Zig-specific compiler argument. Fresh terminals may need absolute tool paths.
The test covers four mappings, preserved default/BGR bits and all invalid
8-bit indices; it does not prove physical panel orientation or SPI completion.

Phase 2 shared-source splash preview:

	cmake --build tools/screen_reference/build/zig --target splash_preview
	python tools/screen_reference/render.py --splash

The preview validates three label bounds and the round mask, not the physical
1.5-second boot transition. Production C++ model/parser tests remain Phase 4.
